{"query": {"id": "20260628174953916577_a37cd617", "handle": "q1", "text": "Ring 
of Nestor gold signet ring Mycenaean discovery provenance 
-site:en.wikipedia.org", "importance": "core"}, "items": [{"id": 
"20260628175055574643_f6316cf2", "type": "Evidence", "text": "书名与副标题：“The
Ring of Nestor: A Glimpse into the Minoan After‑World and a Sepulchral Treasure 
of Gold Signet‑Rings and Bead‑Seals from Thisbê, 
Boeotia”，表明讨论对象是一件被称为“涅斯托耳之戒”的金质印戒及其所在的墓葬宝藏，出
土地为希腊波奥提亚的 Thisbê。", "source_ids": ["20260628175054384544_58f05803"],
"citations": [1]}, {"id": "20260628175055704846_92c1ae10", "type": "Evidence", 
"text": "目录中的部分标题：“I. Sepulchral treasure of gold signet-rings and 
bead-seals from Thisbê, Boeotia” 与 “II. A glimpse into the Minoan 
after‑world”，显示第一部分聚焦 Thisbê 
墓葬宝藏的出土状况和器物，第二部分专论其图像所指涉的米诺斯式来世世界。", 
"source_ids": ["20260628175054384544_58f05803"], "citations": [1]}, {"id": 
"20260628175055804579_614144fe", "type": "Evidence", "text": 
"海德堡数字库的元数据关键词列出：“Nestor; Ring; Minoische Kultur; Thísvi; 
Europe; Greece; 
Kakóvatos”，指明该出版物关联涅斯托耳之戒、米诺斯文化、Thísvi（Thisbê）以及卡科瓦
托斯等相关地名和文化术语。", "source_ids": ["20260628175054384544_58f05803"], 
"citations": [1]}, {"id": "20260628175055898981_9922c96a", "type": "Evidence", 
"text": "数字版说明提供“五幅图版（Tafel 
I–V）”，显示该书附有五个图版单元用于展示戒指实物及印纹等图像资料。", 
"source_ids": ["20260628175054384544_58f05803"], "citations": [1]}, {"id": 
"20260628175055991161_1e2be02f", "type": "Evidence", "text": 
"论文摘要指出：“this famous Mycenaean signet ring of the ‘Tiryns treasure’ was 
discovered in December 1915 by Apostolos Arvanitopoulos in the lower town of 
Tiryns”并说明它是一枚“type IV golden ring”其 hoop being a “thick reed‑hammered 
roll”。", "source_ids": ["20260628175054419348_abfe9748"], "citations": [2]}, 
{"id": "20260628175056078756_49d00ded", "type": "Evidence", "text": 
"论文中将这枚戒指的编目号记为“CMS I, 179”，表明其纳入《Corpus der Minoischen und
Mykenischen Siegel》的第一卷第 179 号条目。", "source_ids": 
["20260628175054419348_abfe9748"], "citations": [2]}, {"id": 
"20260628175056170255_458da968", "type": "Evidence", "text": "Amazon 
商品标题写作：“ʻThe ring of Nestor;̓ a glimpse into the Minoan after‑world, and a
sepulchral treasure of gold signet‑rings and bead‑seals from Thisbê, Boeotia, by
Sir Arthur Evans. With five plates, [Leather Bound]”，确认作者为 Sir Arthur 
Evans 并指出该版本带有五幅图版。", "source_ids": 
["20260628175054455733_7924955e"], "citations": [3]}, {"id": 
"20260628175056264457_03c981d9", "type": "Evidence", "text": "Amazon 
描述中将该书标注为“Leather Bound”且通常说明为按需重印版，显示其为现代再版而非 
1925 年原版。", "source_ids": ["20260628175054455733_7924955e"], "citations": 
[3]}, {"id": "20260628175256899029_a0b6cd96", "type": "Claim", "text": "The 
object known as the Ring of Nestor is a famous Mycenaean gold signet ring 
catalogued as CMS I, 179 in the Corpus der Minoischen und Mykenischen Siegel.", 
"source_ids": ["20260628175054419348_abfe9748"], "citations": [2]}, {"id": 
"20260628175257056682_7218c3cd", "type": "Claim", "text": "Evans classed the 
Ring of Nestor (CMS I, 179) as a type IV golden ring with a hoop formed as a 
thick reed‑hammered roll.", "source_ids": ["20260628175054419348_abfe9748"], 
"citations": [2]}, {"id": "20260628175257147748_c8b85b19", "type": "Claim", 
"text": "The Ring of Nestor (CMS I, 179), a Mycenaean gold signet ring, was 
discovered in December 1915 by archaeologist Apostolos Arvanitopoulos in the 
lower town of Tiryns as part of what Evans called the 'Tiryns treasure'.", 
"source_ids": ["20260628175054419348_abfe9748"], "citations": [2]}, {"id": 
"20260628175257282972_8c0e25d8", "type": "Claim", "text": "Evans described the 
Ring of Nestor and associated gold signet rings and bead‑seals from Thisbê, 
Boeotia as a sepulchral treasure, i.e., a group of burial finds from a funerary 
context.", "source_ids": ["20260628175054384544_58f05803", 
"20260628175054455733_7924955e"], "citations": [1, 3]}, {"id": 
"20260628175257623272_3be77155", "type": "Claim", "text": "In his booklet 'The 
Ring of Nestor: A Glimpse into the Minoan After‑World and a Sepulchral Treasure 
of Gold Signet‑Rings and Bead‑Seals from Thisbê, Boeotia', Sir Arthur Evans 
presented the Ring of Nestor as a gold signet ring associated with a Thisbê, 
Boeotia burial treasure and used its imagery to discuss a Minoan‑style 
afterlife.", "source_ids": ["20260628175054384544_58f05803", 
"20260628175054455733_7924955e"], "citations": [1, 3]}], "offset": 0, "limit": 
20, "total": 13, "next_offset": null}
