"citations": [6]}, {"id": "20260628175225132517_15200d61", "type": "Evidence", 
"text": "书评给出出版信息：“By Sir Arthur Evans. Pp. ii + 75 + 5 plates. 
(London: Macmillan and Co., Ltd., 1925.) 12s. 6d. net.”", "source_ids": 
["20260628175152471196_09198683"], "citations": [6]}, {"id": 
"20260628175225224472_39740f44", "type": "Evidence", "text": "摘要中提到：“Like 
the 'Ring of Nestor', it has a combination of scenes (female individual on a 
boat, altars, sacred trees, and baetyls) tied to the theme of divine …”。", 
"source_ids": ["20260628175221524508_f38f67bb"], "citations": [19]}, {"id": 
"20260628175255315574_1a41993f", "type": "Claim", "text": "The Ring of Nestor is
a large gold signet ring from the sepulchral treasure of gold signet-rings and 
bead-seals discovered at Thisbê in Boeotia; it is characterized by an 
exceptionally large oval bezel and belongs to a group that also includes three 
flattened-cylinder bead-seals and a smaller ring.", "source_ids": 
["20260628175221372282_f25eeb76", "20260628175221412008_d63425e4", 
"20260628175221450188_ed9be685"], "citations": [16, 17, 18]}, {"id": 
"20260628175255540766_c3a7eb4d", "type": "Claim", "text": "The bezel scene of 
the Ring of Nestor depicts a complex ritual or religious composition combining a
female figure on a boat, one or more altars, sacred trees, and baetyls (standing
sacred stones).", "source_ids": ["20260628175152381686_6ef8d955", 
"20260628175221524508_f38f67bb"], "citations": [4, 19]}, {"id": 
"20260628175255764563_841aa8f2", "type": "Claim", "text": "Modern scholarship 
treats the Ring of Nestor as a technically and compositionally highly elaborate 
example of a gold signet ring bearing a miniature religious scene, comparable in
refinement and iconographic complexity to other Minoan or Mycenaean gold signet 
rings with ritual imagery.", "source_ids": ["20260628175152381686_6ef8d955", 
"20260628175221412008_d63425e4", "20260628175221524508_f38f67bb"], "citations": 
[4, 17, 19]}, {"id": "20260628175255876194_6aadb5bd", "type": "Claim", "text": 
"Arthur Evans’s monograph 'The Ring of Nestor; a glimpse into the Minoan 
after-world, and a sepulchral treasure of gold signet-rings and bead-seals from 
Thisbê, Boeotia' (Macmillan, London, 1925; ii + 75 pages and 5 plates) provides 
a systematic description of the Thisbê gold signet rings and bead-seals, 
including the Ring of Nestor, and reproduces the ring’s imagery through 
photographs and line drawings on plates I–V.", "source_ids": 
["20260628175152471196_09198683", "20260628175221412008_d63425e4", 
"20260628175221450188_ed9be685"], "citations": [6, 17, 18]}, {"id": 
"20260628175256152102_8f325161", "type": "Claim", "text": "The Ring of Nestor is
cited and illustrated in Arthur Evans’s 'The Palace of Minos' volume IV, figure 
915b, and is treated in later scholarship as a key example when discussing 
pseudo-Minoan gold signet rings, their large oval bezels, and engraving style in
relation to Bronze Age technical characteristics.", "source_ids": 
["20260628175152381686_6ef8d955", "20260628175221372282_f25eeb76"], "citations":
[4, 16]}, {"id": "20260628175256349636_6f5b507a", "type": "Claim", "text": 
"Type-chronological discussion in modern scholarship associates the Ring of 
Nestor’s large gold signet ring type with use that ceased after the Geometric 
period, implying a tradition of such rings extending from the Bronze Age into 
later eras before falling into disuse.", "source_ids": 
["20260628175221372282_f25eeb76"], "citations": [16]}], "offset": 0, "limit": 
20, "total": 19, "next_offset": null}
