indicating that the article addresses questions of whether the ring is genuine 
and how its imagery is understood.", "source_ids": 
["20260628175152381686_6ef8d955"], "citations": [4]}, {"id": 
"20260628175607491634_c0dd0588", "type": "Evidence", "text": "“This paper 
presents an analysis of the iconography surrounding the ‘Ring of Nestor’ in the 
context of Aegean forgeries and authenticity debates,” suggesting that the paper
considers the ring’s imagery alongside concerns about forgery.", "source_ids": 
["20260628175152381686_6ef8d955"], "citations": [4]}, {"id": 
"20260628175607586675_a1ca3425", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The snippet notes:
“THE signet-ring illustrated in figures 1-3 was presented to the City Art Muse 
St. Louis by Kurt W. Bachstitz in 1924. It is made of bronze ex- FIG. Mycenaean 
...”, indicating a discussion of provenance and a gift to a museum collection.",
"source_ids": ["20260628175221524508_f38f67bb"], "citations": [19]}, {"id": 
"20260628175628976389_49f6c0b6", "type": "Claim", "text": "Arthur J. Evans’s 
1925 monograph “The ring of Nestor. A glimpse into the Minoan after-world and a 
sepulchral treasure of gold signet-rings and bead-seals from Thisbê, Boeotia” 
documents a sepulchral treasure of gold signet-rings and bead-seals discovered 
in a tomb at Thisbê (Thísvi) in Boeotia, Greece, including the object later 
known as the “Ring of Nestor.”", "source_ids": ["20260628175054384544_58f05803",
"20260628175221412008_d63425e4", "20260628175603970924_4fda2a33"], "citations": 
[1, 17, 20]}, {"id": "20260628175629230396_ca0e9f1c", "type": "Claim", "text": 
"In Evans’s monograph, the archaeological context and description of the 
sepulchral treasure from the Thisbê tomb, including the ring later called the 
“Ring of Nestor,” are treated in section I (“Sepulchral treasure of gold 
signet-rings and bead-seals from Thisbê, Boeotia,” pages 1–42), while 
interpretive discussion of a Minoan after-world appears in section II (“A 
glimpse into the Minoan after-world,” pages 43–75).", "source_ids": 
["20260628175054384544_58f05803", "20260628175221412008_d63425e4"], "citations":
[1, 17]}, {"id": "20260628175629424903_88fd227b", "type": "Claim", "text": 
"Evans’s study is accompanied by plates I–V that visually document the gold 
signet-rings and bead-seals from the Thisbê tomb, including the object later 
identified as the “Ring of Nestor,” thereby providing primary visual evidence 
for the ring’s form and imagery.", "source_ids": 
["20260628175054384544_58f05803", "20260628175221412008_d63425e4"], "citations":
[1, 17]}, {"id": "20260628175629592263_8a0fb193", "type": "Claim", "text": 
"Library and digital-library metadata (Heidelberg University Library and Aegeus 
